## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical privacy controls in LLM ops, focusing on implementable redaction, per-tenant policy configuration, and measurable latency impact.

## Key Concepts
- PII detection and redaction via regex rules
- Per-tenant policy configuration with hot-reload
- Data locality: redact before network transfer or on-device when feasible
- Latency budgeting and minimal test coverage for accuracy

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example redaction skeleton
const defaultPIIPatterns = {
  emails: /\b[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\.[A-Za-z]{2,}\b/g,
  phones: /(\+?\d{1,3}[-.\s]?)?(\(?\d{3}\)?|\d{3})[-.\s]?\d{3}[-.\s]?\d{4}/g,
  ssn: /\b\d{3}-\d{2}-\d{4}\b/g
};

function redactPrompt(prompt, tenantRules) {
  const patterns = Object.assign({}, defaultPIIPatterns, tenantRules?.patterns);
  let redacted = prompt;
  for (const key in patterns) {
    redacted = redacted.replace(patterns[key], '[REDACTED]');
  }
  return redacted;
}
```

